## Summary
The Mundaneum in Mons, Belgium, was an early 20th-century project that organized the world's knowledge on millions of index cards, functioning as a precursor to the modern internet. Visiting this historical site can fundamentally change perspectives on everyday technology.

## Key Points
- The Mundaneum was an early analog internet from the 20th century that compiled global knowledge.
- It utilized millions of index cards to store and manage information, demonstrating pre-digital data organization.
- Located in Mons, Belgium, it highlights the evolution of information technology and offers historical insights.


